From: Gyimesi Balázs <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: ecm: accelerate through tag_8021q DSA user ports

With the qca-8021q DSA tagger a switch port reaches its conduit as a
plain 802.1Q VLAN: the port's standalone VLAN, or the bridge VLAN when
the port is bridged. Present such a DSA user port to the accel engine
as a VLAN of the conduit, so the NSS rule carries that VLAN tag on the
conduit interface, as for an ethX.Y VLAN device.

A VLAN upper of a standalone port is a switch VLAN of its own and
reaches the conduit with just its own tag. Ports under a VLAN-aware
bridge are not accelerated: their VLAN depends on the flow.

The VLAN priority lookup now only runs on real VLAN devices.

Signed-off-by: Gyimesi Balázs <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
---
--- a/ecm_interface.c
+++ b/ecm_interface.c
@@ -310,7 +310,35 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(ecm_interface_get_and_hold
  */
 static inline struct net_device *ecm_interface_vlan_real_dev(struct net_device *vlan_dev)
 {
-	return vlan_dev_next_dev(vlan_dev);
+	struct net_device *conduit = ecm_interface_dsa_8021q_conduit(vlan_dev);
+	struct net_device *real_dev;
+	struct dsa_port *dp;
+
+	/*
+	 * A qca-8021q DSA user port is a VLAN of its conduit
+	 */
+	if (conduit)
+		return conduit;
+
+	/*
+	 * A VLAN upper of a standalone qca-8021q DSA port is a switch VLAN of its
+	 * own, which reaches the conduit with just this VLAN tag
+	 */
+	real_dev = vlan_dev_next_dev(vlan_dev);
+	dp = ecm_interface_dsa_8021q_port(real_dev);
+	if (dp && !dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp))
+		return dsa_port_to_conduit(dp);
+
+	return real_dev;
+}
+
+/*
+ * ecm_interface_is_vlan_dev()
+ *	True for a VLAN device, and for a DSA user port that is a VLAN of its conduit
+ */
+static inline bool ecm_interface_is_vlan_dev(struct net_device *dev)
+{
+	return is_vlan_dev(dev) || ecm_interface_dsa_8021q_vid(dev) > 0;
 }
 
